{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggySVXTAbL2Wq15iYKM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hub protocol is clear: a 2v2 basketball match fits `shared-world` (host runs the match). Reading the retrofit guide and the client to see what \"the game on its own\" needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6822,"cache_read_input_tokens":106463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6822},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a","uuid":"2999af6f-7324-4699-8e26-18356e05188b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:27.246Z","request_id":"req_011CggySVJJzkPptZmr9GrHE"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggySVXTAbL2Wq15iYKM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RNcGVcRfiWxVPQQJgoJCcK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=$(cat ~/.cache/plan-x21985c.path); cd $R/hub/ai-hub/lib/hub && cat retrofit.md; echo ======; sed -n 1,140p session.js","description":"Read retrofit guide and the start of session.js"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6822,"cache_read_input_tokens":106463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6822},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a","uuid":"4305d53c-44dc-4bce-8c0d-2a8a0c37b110","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:27.670Z","request_id":"req_011CggySVJJzkPptZmr9GrHE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RNcGVcRfiWxVPQQJgoJCcK":{"command":"R=$(cat ~/.cache/plan-x21985c.path); cd $R/hub/ai-hub/lib/hub && cat retrofit.md; echo ======; sed -n 1,140p session.js","description":"Read retrofit guide and the start of session.js"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNcGVcRfiWxVPQQJgoJCcK","type":"tool_result","content":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n======\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a","uuid":"ee2936e3-2f84-41c6-b0ca-6e961a2ad2b5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:27.748Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy 