{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCKFZ85wQmtvNmTJyEKsKX","type":"tool_result","content":"667:- `rig.debug(r)` †: skeleton overlay for debugging, draws straight into the buffer\n668:- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw into g with (ox, oy) = projected position of the rig's root\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g\n670:- `rig.drawSmear(r, colors = ['#ffffff', '#dff8ff', '#8fe0f2', '#4bb1d4'])` †: motion smear for the current swing, queued in front of the rig\n671:- `rig.hand(which = 'R')`: world position of a hand ('R' holds the weapon): spawn bullets, sparks or thrown things here\n672:- `rig.head()`: world position of the head (for speech bubbles, portraits, halos)\n673:- `rig.kick(v)`: a squash-and-stretch kick: + stretches (a jump), - squashes (a landing, a hit)\n674:- `rig.land(strength = 1)` †: a heavy landing: knees bend deep and spring back over a moment; strength 1 or more drops a hand to the ground (a three-point landing), .3-.6 is a soft one. Call it on the step the body lands\n675:- `rig.solvePose()`: set the joints J from the rig's state this step (update and setPose call it); a clip player may wrap it on one rig: const base = rig.solvePose; rig.solvePose = function () { base.call(this); ...move J... }\n676:- `rig.tip()`: world position of the weapon tip (sword tip, gun muzzle, staff orb)\n677:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0\n678:- `rig.worldOffset(p)`: where a point in the rig's own frame ([forward, right, up]; a joint such as rig.J.head, or one offset from it) sits, in world units from the rig's feet: add rig.x, y, z for the world point, or project it to draw at a joint\n679:- `rig.C`: its colors (skin, hair, cloth, pants, boot, belt, cape, capeIn, metal, hilt, eye, ...), the defaults with o.colors over them; change one and it shows at the next draw\n680:- `rig.J`: its joints this step in its own frame ({ hipL, kneeL, footL, shC, head, handR, ... }; rig.worldOffset(J.handR) gives one in the world)\n681:- `rig.atkZ = 10`: the height of the weapon hand during an attack\n682:- `rig.blink = 2`: seconds to the next blink\n683:- `rig.capeL = null`: the cape's left edge points (null until it has a cape and has moved)\n684:- `rig.capeR = []`: the cape's right edge points\n685:- `rig.dieT`: pose 'die': a stagger, the knees give, then the body topples\n686:- `rig.downW`: how far down it is, 0..1 (state down, pose 'down' or 'die'): it falls faster and faster and gets up steadily\n687:- `rig.expr` †: the face shown ('smile', 'shout', 'angry', 'wince'), or null\n688:- `rig.facing = 0`: the angle it faces, radians\n689:- `rig.hop`: how high an attack's hop lifts it now\n690:- `rig.hurtW = 0`: 0..1, how far into the hurt flinch\n691:- `rig.lastView` †: drawSmear projects the trail with the same view\n692:- `rig.lunge`: how far the body leans into an attack now, world units\n693:- `rig.o`: its options, with the build's proportions and the defaults filled in (size, build, weapon, outfit, ...; legUpper, torso, headR and the other lengths are at size 1)\n694:- `rig.phase = 0`: the walk cycle's phase, radians\n695:- `rig.poseW`: held poses: 'cheer' (item get, victory), 'cast' (both hands forward), 'guard' (fists up), 'kneel', 'crouch', 'wave', 'hips' (hands on hips), and down: 0..1 (knocked flat). stance: 'guard' (fists up while moving) | 'ready' (weapon held forwar\n696:- `rig.reach = 7`: how far it reaches forward\n697:- `rig.spin = 0`: the body's extra turn during a spinning move, radians\n698:- `rig.sq = 0`: squash and stretch, -0.45..0.45 (kick adds to it)\n699:- `rig.sqV = 0`: its speed\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n701:- `rig.trail = []` †: recent points of the blade (or fist) tip, for the swing's smear\n702:- `rig.x = 0`, `rig.y = 0`, `rig.z = 0`: where its feet are (from the last update)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a","uuid":"fb649d4d-4a9a-4800-a0ba-f9f4781ff4b8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:25.260Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"667:- `rig.debug(r)` †: skeleton overlay for debugging, draws straight into the buffer\n668:- `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`: draw into g with (ox, oy) = projected position of the rig's root\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g\n670:- `rig.drawSmear(r, colors = ['#ffffff', '#dff8ff', '#8fe0f2', '#4bb1d4'])` †: motion smear for the current swing, queued in front of the rig\n671:- `rig.hand(which = 'R')`: world position of a hand ('R' holds the weapon): spawn bullets, sparks or thrown things here\n672:- `rig.head()`: world position of the head (for speech bubbles, portraits, halos)\n673:- `rig.kick(v)`: a squash-and-stretch kick: + stretches (a jump), - squashes (a landing, a hit)\n674:- `rig.land(strength = 1)` †: a heavy landing: knees bend deep and spring back over a moment; strength 1 or more drops a hand to the ground (a three-point landing), .3-.6 is a soft one. Call it on the step the body lands\n675:- `rig.solvePose()`: set the joints J from the rig's state this step (update and setPose call it); a clip player may wrap it on one rig: const base = rig.solvePose; rig.solvePose = function () { base.call(this); ...move J... }\n676:- `rig.tip()`: w