{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JHRfkveTfpqP5MBJ6DhosD","type":"tool_result","content":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in p\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the \n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1176:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n1177:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n1183:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [units] }: a threat map\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a","uuid":"7449c267-fe9b-4c89-9ebe-dfb0cd51b57f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:17.933Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in p\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the \n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1176:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n1177:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n1183:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [units] }: a threat map","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JHRfkveTfpqP5MBJ6DhosD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
