{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PCycSNRVLqqzjFsBa6e7kF","type":"tool_result","content":"class Dialog {\n  /** new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types\n   *  its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game */\n    this.game = game;\n    /** speed: letters typed per second; lines: text lines per page; place: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'; color: the\n     *  text's color; nameColor: the speaker's name's color; voice: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null\n     *  for silence); bg, border: the box's colors; vars: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first) */\n    Object.assign(this, { speed: 50, lines: 3, place: 'bottom', color: '#ffffff', nameColor: '#ffd36a', voice: 'text', bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', vars: null }, o);\n    /** open: true while it shows; pages: the text wrapped into pages of lines; i: the page shown; shown: letters\n     *  typed so far on it; choice: the choice under the cursor */\n    this.open = false; this.pages = []; this.i = 0; this.shown = 0; this.choice = 0;\n  }\n  /** where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null */\n  choiceAt(i) { if (!this.open || !this.choices || this.typing || this.i < this.pages.length - 1 || !this.choices[i]) return null; const d = this._dims(), b = this._cbox(d); return [Math.round(b.x + b.w / 2), Math.round(b.y + 3 + (i + .5) * d.lh)]; }\n  // the choices' box, over the box's right end\n  _cbox(d) { const w = Math.max(...this.choices.map(c => E.font.width(c))) + 20, h = this.choices.length * d.lh + 7; return { x: d.x + d.w - w - 2, y: d.y - h - 2, w, h }; }\n7538:    /** presets: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one; song: the music\n7617:    if (!p) { warn('sfx:' + what, 'unknown sound \"' + what + '\". Presets: ' + Object.keys(this.presets).join(', ') + ' (or audio.define(name, voice))'); return; }\n7627:  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\n8956:    if (this.voice && Math.floor(this.shown) > prev && (this._blip++ % 2 === 0)) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice);\n12953:    this.game = game; this.song = o.song; this.lanes = o.lanes || ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']; this.windows = Object.assign({ perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 }, o.windows); this.lead = o.l\n13015:      if (n.call) { if (!n.played && (n.step - s) * spb < .1) { n.played = true; A.sfx(Object.assign({ freq: CALL[n.lane % CALL.length] }, this.voice), { step: n.step }); } if (!n.j && s >= n.st\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a l\n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (tal\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1118:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1119:- `talk.game`: its game\n1120:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1121:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1122:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1123:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1124:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1125:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1126:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1127:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1128:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1129:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n1130:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom\n1131:- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n1132:- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n1133:- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a","uuid":"f0a96c1c-acf5-4de3-85ae-af1430de3b4d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:10:05.306Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"class Dialog {\n  /** new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types\n   *  its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game */\n    this.game = game;\n    /** speed: letters typed per second; lines: text lines per page; place: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'; color: the\n     *  text's color; nameColor: the speaker's name's color; voice: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null\n     *  for silence); bg, border: the box's colors; vars: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first) */\n    Object.assign(this, { speed: 50, lines: 3, place: 'bottom', color: '#ffffff', nameColor: '#ffd36a', voice: 'text', bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', vars: null }, o);\n    /** open: true while it shows; pages: the text wrapped into pages of lines; i: the page shown; shown: lett